  "focusTag": "Static Stretching, No Kit",
  "intro": [
    "Static stretching with no kit at all, for the days you do not have a roller or do not want one.",
    "These belong after training or on a rest day, never in the ten minutes before you play. Held long enough to matter, a stretch takes a little edge off how forcefully a muscle contracts for the next hour or so — exactly what you want tonight and exactly what you do not want before a match."
  ],
  "before": [
    {
      "label": "Stop and get it looked at",
      "text": "Sharp pain, pins and needles, or anything running down a leg or an arm isn't a stretch, so stop that one."
    },
    {
      "label": "Leave out",
      "text": "If a groin or a hamstring is still sore from playing, leave the hamstring and butterfly stretches out."
    },
    {
      "label": "Swollen calf",
      "text": "If one calf is swollen, warm or tender and you didn't strain it playing, see a doctor the same day."
    }
  ],
